## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a practical, low-latency perception and manipulation system that must rapidly adapt to new furniture models while maintaining consistent performance across different camera configurations—a critical constraint in consumer robotics applications.

## Key Concepts
- 6-DoF pose estimation from monocular RGB
- 5-shot on-device adaptation strategies
- Cross-camera intrinsics handling techniques
- Synthetic-to-real data augmentation approaches
- Embedded GPU latency optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: estimate pose with adaptation
function estimatePoseWithAdaptation(rgbFrame, newFurnitureSamples) {
  // Detect furniture in RGB frame
  const detections = furnitureDetector.predict(rgbFrame);

  // Adapt to new furniture with 5-shot learning
  if (newFurnitureSamples.length >= 5) {
    metaLearner.adapt(newFurnitureSamples);
  }

  // Estimate 6-DoF pose using PnP
  const poses = detections.map(detection => 
    solvePnP(detection.keypoints, detection.3dModel, normalizedIntrinsics)
  );

  return { poses, detections };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates real-time monocular computer vision for avatar-driven video conferencing, with emphasis on three critical constraints: sub-30ms latency for natural interaction, on-device privacy for user trust, and rapid on-device adaptation for personalized gesture vocabularies. Success requires co-designing efficient models, privacy-preserving pipelines, and lightweight adaptation mechanisms—skills essential for building consumer-grade AR/VR experiences at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular landmark detection, gesture recognition, and avatar rig mapping
- Edge latency budgets and resource-aware model architectures
- Few-shot on-device adaptation using synthetic and real data
- Privacy-by-design constraints and rigorous evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton of the avatar estimator outline
class AvatarEstimator {
  constructor(model) {
    this.model = model;
    this.buffer = [];
  }

  infer(frame) {
    const landmarks = this.model.detect(frame);
    const avatarParams = this.mapToAvatar(landmarks);
    return avatarParams;
  }

  mapToAvatar(landmarks) {
    // Map 2D landmarks to 3D avatar rig parameters
    return {
      blendShapes: this.computeBlendShapes(landmarks),
      handPose: this.estimateHandPose(landmarks)
    };
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical monocular depth reasoning and tracking in a simple inspection setting.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth proxy with known geometry
- Lightweight detectors, on-device adaptation
- Temporal tracking and data efficiency

## Code Example
```javascript
function projectTo3D(bbox, sheetDims, intrinsics) {
  // heuristic: depth proxy from vertical size and known sheet height
  const heightPx = bbox.height;
  const Z = (sheetDims.height * intrinsics.fy) / heightPx;
  return {X: 0, Y: 0, Z};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would occlusion or specular glare affect depth proxy? how to mitigate?
- How would you measure success and compare to a stereo baseline?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests system-level thinking for 3D reconstruction under dynamic scenes and edge-runtime constraints, plus evaluation rigor.

## Key Concepts

- Dense 3D representation (TSDF) with dynamic masking
- Lightweight pose estimation and masked fusion
- Dynamic voxel confidence and decay for occlusions
- Edge latency targets and robust evaluation metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: update TSDF with dynamic masking
function updateVoxelTSDF(voxel, depth, pose, isDynamic) {
  if (isDynamic) return; // skip static updates for dynamic voxels until confirmed
  const sdf = projectDepthToVoxel(depth, pose, voxel.coord);
  voxel.tsdf = (voxel.tsdf * voxel.weight + sdf) / (voxel.weight + 1);
  voxel.weight += 1;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you integrate semantic priors to improve dynamic masking in cluttered warehouses?
- What ablation model would you run to measure the impact of dynamic masking on map quality and drift over 5 seconds?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model non-rigid objects and integrate deformation estimation with robotic manipulation under strict latency constraints. It also probes on-device few-shot adaptation and data strategy across synthetic and real data.

## Key Concepts
- Non-rigid pose + deformation
- Photometric, silhouette, and temporal losses
- Differentiable cloth priors for realism
- Edge-optimized, multi-branch architecture
- Lightweight 5-shot on-device adaptation

## Code Example
