## Why This Is Asked
Introduces a new angle: multi-sensor fusion with event cameras for high-dynamic scenes. Assesses architectural discipline and concrete trade-offs for low latency and on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Event cameras and RGB fusion
- 3D voxel grids and lightweight transformers
- On-device 5-shot adaptation and object priors
- Temporal consistency and occlusion handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code: fuse RGB features with events, then predict pose and mask
function forward(rgbFrame, events, priors){
  const rgbFeat = rgbBackbone(rgbFrame);
  const evtFeat = eventBackbone(events);
  const fused = fuse3D(rgbFeat, evtFeat);
  const pose = poseHead(fused, priors);
  const mask = segHead(fused);
  return {pose, mask};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design synthetic data generation to cover unseen shapes with realistic event streams?
- What debugging metrics would help you diagnose latency vs. accuracy bottlenecks on edge hardware?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses on-device CV design, latency budgeting, and robust 3D human pose estimation for safety-critical driving.

## Key Concepts
- On-device real-time inference with a lightweight backbone
- 2D-to-3D pose reconstruction and Kalman filtering
- Self-supervised pretraining from unlabeled video
- Robustness to occlusion and adverse weather
- Quantization and latency accounting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline
class PedestrianPoseEstimator {
  constructor() { /* load detector, 3D head, PnP module, tracker */ }
  forward(frame) {
    const keypoints2D = this.detector.detect(frame)
    const pose3D = this.poseHead.estimate(keypoints2D)
    const pose6DoF = differentiablePnP(pose3D, this.cameraIntrinsics)
    return this.tracker.update(pose6DoF)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-pedestrian tracking with identity preservation?
- What failure modes are most critical in heavy rain and how would you mitigate them?
